y that lets you see"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What color are your eyes?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le01ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "address"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "where you live"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What is your address?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le01ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "black"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the darkest color"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "My hair is black."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le01ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "glasses"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a frame with lenses to help you see"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wear glasses."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le01ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "parents"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "mother and father"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is my parents' address too."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le01ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Describing People"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To describe someone, you use adjectives. <br/>Adjectives are words that describe a person.<br/> If two adjectives describe a person, use <span class=\"strong\">and</span> to link the adjectives. <br/>If there are more than two adjectives, use commas, then use <span class=\"strong\">and</span> before the last adjective."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"italic\">The <span class =\"strong\">kind</span> girl.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"italic\">The <span class =\"strong\">kind</span> girl is <span class =\"strong\">short</span> and <span class =\"strong\">blonde</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"italic\">He is <span class =\"strong\">tall</span>, <span class =\"strong\">smart</span> and <span class =\"strong\">handsome</span>.</span>"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le01ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Short Vowel Sounds"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A short vowel happens when a vowel is followed by a consonant. A vowel is usually short when there is only one vowel in a word. For example: <span class=\"italic\">cat</span> or <span class=\"italic\">dog</span>. <br><br>The most common sound for each vowel is its \u201cshort\u201d sound: </br></br><li>the a sound as in apple, can, or mat </br><li>the e sound as in elephant, leg, or rent </br><li>the i sound as in insect, pin, or lift  </br><li> the o sound as in ostrich, October, or motto </br> <li>the u sound as in umbrella, pun, or uncle"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ask a friend or family member about their personal information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Complete the table."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Name:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Last Name:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Address:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Date of Birth:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"